// Title: Outlook EnableUnsafeClientMailRules Setting Enabled
// Sigma ID: 55f0a3a1-846e-40eb-8273-677371b8d912
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Markus Neis, Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2018-12-27 | Modified: 2023-02-09
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1059, T1202
// Description: Detects an attacker trying to enable the outlook security setting "EnableUnsafeClientMailRules"
//   which allows outlook to run applications or execute macros
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.fireeye.com/blog/threat-research/2018/12/overruled-containing-a-potentially-destructive-adversary.html
//   - https://speakerdeck.com/heirhabarov/hunting-for-persistence-via-microsoft-exchange-server-or-outlook?slide=44
//   - https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/topic/how-to-control-the-rule-actions-to-start-an-application-or-run-a-macro-in-outlook-2016-and-outlook-2013-e4964b72-173c-959d-5d7b-ead562979048
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_office_outlook_enable_unsafe_client_mail_rules.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "\\Outlook\\Security\\EnableUnsafeClientMailRules"
